Confirmed — this is an IDOR (broken object-level authorization) bug. `req.user.accountId` is available on every request (set in `auth.js`), but the write queries key off `req.params.id`/`req.params.id` alone with no ownership check, so any authenticated user can modify or cancel another account's data by guessing/incrementing an id.

