Two layers worth separating: generic HTTP access logs, and an audit trail for the mutations these routes perform (account edits, deletes, order cancels touch billing/account data, so "who did what to which id" matters more than raw request logging here).

**1. Mount it centrally in app.js, not per-route**

Add one middleware after `app.use(sessionUser)` (app.js:11) and before the route mounts (app.js:13-14), so it automatically covers every handler in accounts.js and orders.js without touching those files:

```js
